  "id": "BIT-elasticsearch-2026-102404",
  "summary": "Uncontrolled Resource Consumption in Elasticsearch Leading to Denial of Service",
  "details": "Uncontrolled Resource Consumption (CWE-400) in Elasticsearch can lead to denial of service via Excessive Allocation (CAPEC-130). A low-privileged authenticated user can submit a specially crafted query that causes uncontrolled memory growth in the query processing engine, resulting in an out-of-memory condition that terminates the Elasticsearch node. The condition can be triggered repeatedly, including by queries embedded in shared resources, causing persistent cluster unavailability.",
